 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 631874,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>The equivalent functions below model the height of a projectile in meters, <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> seconds after launch.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"h(t)=-8t^2+27t+20\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;h(t)=(-8t−5)(t−4)\">h(t)=-8t^2+27t+20\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;h(t)=(-8t−5)(t−4)</span></p>\n<p>Without graphing, determine at what time the height of the object is 0 meters (when the object is on the ground).</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1223104,
     "content_html": "8 seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223107,
     "content_html": "4 seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223105,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac {5}{8}\">\\frac {5}{8}</span> seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223106,
     "content_html": "0 seconds"
    }
   ],
